      "parameters": {
        "mode": "retrieve-as-tool",
        "toolDescription": "This tool performs semantic similarity searches on a vector database containing laptop information. It finds laptops that match user queries based on semantic meaning rather than exact keyword matching.\n\nDatabase Content\n\nThe database contains laptops with information such as:\n\nLaptop product names\n\nBrands and product series\n\nPrimary usage categories (study, office work, gaming, graphic design, programming, portability, etc.)\n\nKey features and notable characteristics (high-quality display, long battery life, 120Hz refresh rate, OLED screen, lightweight design, strong performance, etc.)\n\nScreen sizes (in inches)\n\nWeight (in kilograms)\n\nCPU types (Apple M-series, Intel Core i5/i7/i9, Intel Core Ultra, AMD Ryzen series, etc.)\n\nRAM capacities\n\nStorage capacities\n\nPricing in VND\n\nAll records are embedded using the OpenAI Embeddings node and stored inside the MongoDB Atlas Vector Store for semantic retrieval.\n\nWhen to Use\n\nUse this tool to find relevant laptop suggestions based on natural language queries such as:\n\n“Recommend a laptop for IT students under 20 million VND.”\n\n“Find a lightweight laptop for studying, preferably 14 inches.”\n\n“Is there any gaming laptop in the 25–30 million VND range?”\n\n“Show me laptops with 32GB RAM suitable for graphic design.”\n\n“Compare a few MacBook options for programming.”\n\nThe tool returns the 5 most semantically similar laptops from the database, helping users quickly discover models that best match their needs, preferences, and requirements.",
